WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Economic pressures forced Thomas Ruyant to withdraw from the route to RUM this week as IMOCA project costs hit 10 million euros. This is Offshore North Episode 12. Every four years, a small number of sailors set out alone to sail nonstop around the world, and one Canadian is working toward becoming the first to finish that race. On the Canadian boat as of November 2nd, 2026, the team's YB tracker shows Emira for alongside in Gospor UK in Portsmouth Harbor. Canada Ocean Racing posted a YouTube video on 31 October

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.420
in which Scott Shawier breaks down the route to RUM-20026 start. He covers weather routing,

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.000
wind patterns, and the tactical choices facing the fleet in the first days.

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:44.400
Shawier notes the race runs from St. Mallow to Guadalupe and explains how pressure systems

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.200
and routing decisions shape the early stages even though he is not competing.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.880
The video is the campaign's most recent public output and focuses on the conditions the 115

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:56.360
boat fleet faced after the first November start.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:01.300
Shawyer describes the light north easterly winds at the gun and the mandatory mark at

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.960
Cap Frehelle, 16 nautical miles from the line.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:08.020
He walks through how the fleet would position for the passage toward the Isles of Silly

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.240
and Fastnet Rock in the opening hours.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:15.180
The analysis draws on his own offshore experience to highlight the trade-off skippers' face when

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:17.100
the first systems move through the English channel.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:22.300
That analysis matters because Shawyer's next confirmed race is the double-handed RORC

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:25.500
transatlantic in January 2027 on the same boat.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:30.560
Oceans time and routing practice now directly support the longer-term goal of a solo vende

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.900
globe finish in 2028, the first by any Canadian.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:38.180
The video gives listeners a direct window into the decision-making that will matter when

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:40.680
Shawier returns to solo racing on Emira 4.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:46.678
Now at the fleet, the route to Rums started on 1st November with 115 solo boats leaving

00:01:46.678 --> 00:01:48.878
Saint Malo in light north-easterly winds.

00:01:49.398 --> 00:01:53.858
Veilette Dorange on initiatives carried collided with Romain Piliard's trimorant, used it

00:01:53.858 --> 00:01:58.798
again near yield to Brayhat, shortly after the start, damaging her starboard foil. Both

00:01:58.798 --> 00:02:03.238
boats diverted to Roscoff for repairs while the skippers remained unhurt. The incident

00:02:03.238 --> 00:02:07.738
shows how quickly a single collision can remove a top 10 contender from contention in a solo

00:02:07.738 --> 00:02:12.838
race where every hour of lost time compounds. Dorange had been running inside the top 10

00:02:12.838 --> 00:02:17.718
in the IMOCA class in the early miles. Technical stops are permitted without penalty in

00:02:17.718 --> 00:02:23.646
the first 150 miles, yet the foil damage still threatens her overall result. Thomas Ruyant

00:02:23.646 --> 00:02:27.286
withdrew from the route to rum before the start because he could not close his budget.

00:02:27.766 --> 00:02:32.906
The article reports IMOCA project costs have risen to 10 million euros, driven by design,

00:02:33.126 --> 00:02:37.846
materials, and insurance. With sponsorship now the sole revenue source and no television or

00:02:37.846 --> 00:02:43.006
ticket income to offset shortfalls. Ruant said he is unwilling to race at any cost and expects

00:02:43.006 --> 00:02:47.506
difficult months ahead. The withdrawal leaves the defending champions boat on the dock and

00:02:47.506 --> 00:02:52.126
illustrates how rising entry costs can sideline experience campaigns even when interest exists.

00:02:52.766 --> 00:02:57.966
Guillaume Goose of the Center to draw a economy to sport noted that some sponsors are renewing

00:02:57.966 --> 00:03:00.806
partnerships while others face broader economic uncertainty.

00:03:01.086 --> 00:03:05.586
He compared the 10 million-year-old figure to the cost of shirt sponsorship for a top-leg

00:03:05.586 --> 00:03:06.546
unfootball club.

00:03:07.026 --> 00:03:11.266
The piece frames the root-do-rum as a test case for whether the class can sustain its current

00:03:11.266 --> 00:03:13.026
scale without diversified revenue.

00:03:14.038 --> 00:03:18.358
Anthony Martian stopped his actual ultim-4 after a rudder failure early in the race.

00:03:18.358 --> 00:03:23.238
The incident adds to a pattern of mechanical issues appearing in the first days and forces

00:03:23.238 --> 00:03:25.458
another skipper out of a race already underway.

00:03:26.058 --> 00:03:30.218
Marshan had been running near the front of the ultim class alongside Tom LaPersche on

00:03:30.218 --> 00:03:35.958
SVR Lazartig and Armel LaClayak on Bonk Popular 11 after the Cap Frey Hellmark.

00:03:36.418 --> 00:03:40.278
The failure occurred in the same window when the fleet was still compact and maneuvering

00:03:40.278 --> 00:03:41.598
frequently in building winds.

00:03:42.078 --> 00:03:43.278
Time for plane sailing.

00:03:43.278 --> 00:03:48.763
and IMOCA campaigns annual operating budget typically runs between 4 and 5

00:03:48.763 --> 00:03:52.823
million euros once a new boat is in the water. That figure covers the permanent

00:03:52.823 --> 00:03:57.423
short-team spare parts, insurance, travel to events, and the constant cycle of

00:03:57.423 --> 00:04:01.203
repairs that follows every offshore race. The number comes from repeated

00:04:01.203 --> 00:04:05.003
reporting across the class and explains why title sponsorship is the only

00:04:05.003 --> 00:04:09.203
realistic funding model. There are no television rights or gate receipts to spread

00:04:09.203 --> 00:04:13.643
the load. When a sponsor pulls out or a budget gap appears, the entire season

00:04:13.643 --> 00:04:17.123
can collapse because no secondary revenue streams exist to bridge it.

00:04:17.503 --> 00:04:21.843
The 10 million euro project costs cited this week is the capital outlay for the boat itself.

00:04:22.463 --> 00:04:26.723
The 4-5 million figure is what it then costs to keep that boat racing year after year.

00:04:27.363 --> 00:04:32.063
Insurance alone can represent 9-10% of the build price, and every major component from

00:04:32.063 --> 00:04:35.283
foils to mass requires dedicated spares and specialist labor.

00:04:35.663 --> 00:04:39.903
The model leaves teams exposed when economic conditions tighten, has seen in the route

00:04:39.903 --> 00:04:46.397
to rum withdrawals this season and the countdown. 741 days remain until the Vendée Globe start

00:04:46.397 --> 00:04:52.417
on November 12th, 2028. The campaign's next concrete milestone is the RORC transatlantic

00:04:52.417 --> 00:04:58.277
race start on January 10th, 2027 from Marina, Lanzarote. That's your week in offshore racing.

00:04:58.797 --> 00:05:02.357
